sequenceDiagram
    %% ============================================================
    %% PARTICIPANTS
    %% ============================================================
    participant U as User
    participant UI as User Interface (UIX)
    participant DQP as Data Pre-Processing & Quality (DQP)
    participant MT as Matching Engine (MT - 16 Steps)
    participant HR as Human Reasoning Layer (HRL)
    participant LS as Learning & Scoring (LS)
    participant BE as Banking Exceptions (BE)
    participant HVP as Safety Layer (HVP/HVPY/SW)
    participant REP as Reporting & Audit (REP)
    participant SP as System Philosophy (SP - Integrity, Transparency, Adaptability, Explainability)

    %% ============================================================
    %% STAGE 1: INPUT + VALIDATION
    %% ============================================================
    U->>UI: Upload Bank Statement & Ledger Extracts
    UI->>DQP: Start Validation & Pre-Processing
    DQP->>DQP: Normalize Dates, Amounts, Text (DQP-01)
    DQP->>DQP: Cleanse Duplicates, Missing Fields (DQP-02)
    DQP->>DQP: Validate Data Integrity (DQP-03)
    DQP-->>UI: Send Diagnostics Report
    U->>UI: Review & (Optionally) Correct Errors
    DQP-->>UI: Final Valid Dataset Ready

    %% ============================================================
    %% STAGE 2: SMART TAGGING & CONTEXT INITIALIZATION
    %% ============================================================
    UI->>HR: Send Dataset for Context Understanding
    HR->>HR: Apply Smart Tagging (payer/payee, category, intent)
    HR-->>MT: Return Tagged Dataset + Context Map
    LS->>MT: Provide Previous Fingerprints & Rule Context
    SP-->>MT: Enforce Integrity Checks Pre-Matching

    %% ============================================================
    %% STAGE 3: MATCHING ENGINE (16 Steps)
    %% ============================================================

    %% Step 1: Exact Match
    MT->>MT: Match by Amount & Date (Exact Thresholds)
    MT->>HVP: Check High-Value (HVP-01)
    HVP-->>MT: Require Manual Confirmation if Flagged
    HR-->>MT: Validate Context of Exact Matches (HR-01)

    %% Step 2: Near-Exact Match
    MT->>MT: Match with ±1 Day, Minor Amount Rounding (TH)
    HR-->>MT: Add Reasoning Context (HR-02)
    LS->>MT: Apply Weighted Scoring for Similarity (LS-01)
    MT-->>UI: Show Near-Exact Matches for Quick Approval
    U->>UI: Approve or Reject Matches

    %% Step 3: Bank Fees
    MT->>MT: Identify Small Debits Matching Fee Patterns
    HR->>HR: Detect Service Fee or Charge Tags
    HR-->>MT: Mark as “Fee-Type Match” with Context Reason
    MT->>HVP: Verify if Fee is Legit & Expected
    HVP-->>MT: Approved / Flagged for User Review

    %% Step 4: Interest Recognition
    MT->>MT: Detect Credit Transactions Matching “Interest” Tags
    HR->>HR: Context Validation (Bank → Ledger Interest Income)
    HR-->>MT: Confirm Financially Logical Context
    MT-->>UI: Present Interest Matches
    U->>UI: Confirm or Reject

    %% Step 5: Split Payments (1→Many)
    MT->>MT: Group Multiple Ledger Entries ≈ One Bank Debit
    HR->>MT: Analyze Logical Relationship of Entries (same payer)
    LS->>MT: Optimize Group Confidence (Hungarian/Score)
    MT-->>UI: Suggest Grouped Match
    U->>UI: Approve or Reclassify Group

    %% Step 6: Group Receipts (Many→1)
    MT->>MT: Identify Multiple Bank Credits ≈ One Ledger Record
    HR->>MT: Verify Common Source or Purpose
    LS->>MT: Apply Group Scoring
    MT-->>UI: Show Group Receipts for Validation
    U->>UI: Confirm or Split Further

    %% Step 7: Duplicate Postings
    MT->>BE: Detect Duplicates (Bank or Ledger)
    BE-->>MT: Mark as Duplicate & Isolate
    HR-->>MT: Explain via Context (system repost / reversal)
    UI->>U: Display Duplicate Alerts
    U->>UI: Accept / Resolve / Mark as Known Error

    %% Step 8: Reversals
    MT->>BE: Find Opposite Sign & Similar Amount
    HR->>MT: Identify Root Transaction of Reversal
    BE-->>MT: Classify as Reversal Pair
    MT-->>UI: Present Reversal Summary
    U->>UI: Approve / Adjust if Partial Reversal

    %% Step 9: Timing Difference
    MT->>BE: Compare Date Offsets (e.g., weekend or holiday drift)
    HR->>MT: Contextual Reason — “Delayed Clearing”
    BE-->>MT: Annotate Cause (Timing Difference)
    MT-->>UI: Show Pending Matches Waiting Posting
    U->>UI: Accept / Defer

    %% Step 10: Pending Entries
    MT->>BE: Identify Ledger-Only or Bank-Only Pending Items
    HR->>MT: Reason on Posting Delay or Manual Entry Needed
    MT-->>UI: Suggest Action: “Await Future Statement” / “Create Entry”
    U->>UI: Take Decision or Skip

    %% Step 11: Multi-Currency Adjustments
    MT->>BE: Identify FX Difference Transactions
    HR->>MT: Compute Conversion Impact, Rate Context
    BE-->>MT: Annotate Currency Difference
    MT-->>UI: Show FX Adjusted Matches
    U->>UI: Validate or Confirm Rate

    %% Step 12: High-Volume Payers
    MT->>HR: Recognize Repeated Payer Patterns
    HR-->>MT: Boost Confidence on Pattern-Based Matches
    LS->>MT: Record Pattern Fingerprints (LS-03)
    HVP->>MT: Review for Unusual Frequency (Fraud Check)
    U->>UI: Review Bulk Matches for Confirmation

    %% Step 13: High-Value Transactions
    MT->>HVP: Scan All High-Value Threshold Breaches
    HVP-->>MT: Lock Match for Manual Review
    HR->>MT: Context Check — Validate Payee / Purpose
    MT-->>UI: Show High-Value Review Panel
    U->>UI: Approve / Reject / Annotate Reason

    %% Step 14: Unmatched Items
    MT->>BE: Collect Remaining Unmatched Bank/Ledger Entries
    BE-->>MT: Categorize Reasons (Timing, Missing, Fee, Data Error)
    HR->>MT: Add Contextual Reasoning Summary
    MT-->>UI: Display Unmatched List for User Action
    U->>UI: Approve Explanation or Trigger Re-Run

    %% Step 15: Auto-Categorized Exceptions
    MT->>BE: Apply Learned Rules from LS (auto-detect known mismatches)
    BE-->>MT: Label Transactions Based on History
    HR->>MT: Review Auto-Categorization
    MT-->>UI: Show Summary of Auto-Classified Exceptions
    U->>UI: Confirm Auto-Classification

    %% Step 16: Final Validation
    MT->>MT: Reconcile Coverage Report (matched + unmatched)
    HR->>MT: Perform Human Reasoning Consistency Check
    LS->>MT: Compute Final Accuracy & Confidence Scores
    HVP->>MT: Ensure All High-Value/Volume Items Manually Approved
    SP-->>MT: Apply Integrity Validation (Explainability & Trace)
    MT-->>UI: Send Final Match State (Converged)

    %% ============================================================
    %% STAGE 4: USER REVIEW LOOP & LEARNING
    %% ============================================================
    UI->>U: Display Convergence Dashboard (Matched %, Pending %, Confidence)
    U->>UI: Approve / Adjust / Reclassify
    UI->>LS: Log User Actions & Feedback
    LS->>LS: Update Fingerprints & Rule Weights
    LS-->>MT: Send Updated Threshold Context
    MT->>HR: Update Contextal Memory with Patterns

    %% ============================================================
    %% STAGE 5: FINALIZATION & REPORTING
    %% ============================================================
    MT->>REP: Submit Final Matched + Unmatched Records
    HR->>REP: Submit Context & Reasoning Notes
    LS->>REP: Submit Updated Learning Artifacts
    HVP->>REP: Submit Audit of Protected Transactions
    SP->>REP: Verify Traceability & Integrity
    REP-->>UI: Generate Final Reconciliation Report
    UI-->>U: Deliver Report, Analytics, & Audit Log

    %% ============================================================
    %% STAGE 6: CONTINUOUS IMPROVEMENT LOOP
    %% ============================================================
    LS->>HR: Feed Learning into Context Model
    HR->>LS: Feed Context into Learning Model
    LS-->>REP: Save Updated Model Version
    REP-->>All: Close Reconciliation Run (Versioned Snapshot)
